      ":question/problem": "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(3) \\\\ 2+(6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(3)^2+(8)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{73} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{73}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{73}}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{73}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{73}}{73} \\\\ \\frac{8 \\sqrt{73}}{73}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
